Package: nomologR
Type: Package
Title: Guided Scale Development and Construct Validation
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(
      "Joshua", "Uhalt",
      email = "Josh.Uhalt@gmail.com",
      role = c("aut", "cre")
    )
  )
Description: Provides an evidence-guided workflow for empirical scale development
    and construct validation, designed for graduate students and researchers.
    The package helps users examine item performance, dimensionality,
    measurement models, reliability, convergent and discriminant evidence,
    measurement invariance, and theory-specified nomological networks in the
    sense of Cronbach and Meehl (1955) <doi:10.1037/h0040957>. Methods are
    documented from historical to contemporary practice with literature
    references, and simulated teaching datasets with known population models
    accompany the examples. Following calls for transparent measurement
    practice such as Flake, Pek, and Hehman (2017)
    <doi:10.1177/1948550617693063>, it emphasizes transparent diagnostics,
    reproducible decision logging, and teaching-oriented guidance rather than
    automatic item deletion or binary declarations that a measure is valid.
